<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Specification</title></head><body><pre> Specification AI Chatbot - General Knowledge Feature Functional Specification Document (Enhanced)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Overview This feature aims to develop an AI chatbot capable of answering general awareness questions within a conversational interface, enabling users to quickly obtain information on various topics. The chatbot will also consider the context of previous questions and responses to provide more accurate and relevant answers.

2. User Stories
    - As a user, I want to initiate a conversation with the chatbot, so that I can start asking questions.
    - As a user, I want to ask a question, so that I can receive an accurate and relevant response.
    - As a user, I want to ask follow-up questions based on the chatbot's response, so that I can gather more information.
    - As a user, I want to end the conversation with the chatbot, so that I can free up resources or move on to other tasks.
    - As a user, I want to provide feedback on the chatbot's responses, so that my suggestions can be used to improve the chatbot's performance and user satisfaction.

3. Functional Requirements
    - SHALL recognize and respond accurately to a wide range of general knowledge questions.
    - SHALL implement natural language processing capabilities to understand user queries effectively.
    - SHOULD provide explanations or examples to support answers, where applicable.
    - SHOULD offer a feedback mechanism, enabling users to rate the responses and suggest improvements.
    - MAY offer multiple choices for answering complex questions, with the correct answer indicated.
    - MAY suggest relevant resources or further reading, if available.
    - SHOULD consider the context of previous questions and responses to provide more accurate and relevant answers.

4. User Workflows
    ...

5. UI/UX Considerations
    ...

6. Data Requirements
    ...

7. Integration Points
